.SH NAME
git-work-flow-rm - Remove a flow from the local repository


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work flow rm NAME [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a flow's local ref. This is local: the flow comes back on the next
pull. The replicated removal is archive.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rm


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work-flow(1)\fP
